Package: intel-crashlog
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Static-Built-Using: ${Static-Built-Using}
Description: Extract and decode Intel Crash Log records
 Modern Intel SoCs automatically record hardware state during fatal crashes,
 such as machine check exceptions, triple faults or unexpected resets, into
 on-die memory. When valid records are present during boot, the firmware copies
 them into the ACPI Boot Error Record Table so that the operating system can
 retrieve them.
 .
 This package provides iclg, a command line tool that extracts those records
 from the running platform and decodes them into human readable JSON. It can
 also triage records, list the collection sources available on the platform and
 enable, disable or trigger a collection on demand.

Package: libintel-crashlog1
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Static-Built-Using: ${Static-Built-Using}
Description: Library to extract and decode Intel Crash Log records
 Modern Intel SoCs automatically record hardware state during fatal crashes,
 such as machine check exceptions, triple faults or unexpected resets, into
 on-die memory.
 .
 This package provides the shared library used to extract Crash Log records
 from a platform and to decode them into a register tree, together with the
 product specific collateral required for decoding.

Package: libintel-crashlog-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
# Multi-Arch: same requires the files to be byte identical on every architecture. The headers are
# generated by cbindgen, which maps the Rust types to fixed width C types and does not vary with the
# architecture, and the pkg-config file only differs in the multiarch path, which is part of the
# file name. Confirm this with a diff between two architectures when the FFI surface changes.
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 libintel-crashlog1 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Library to extract and decode Intel Crash Log records - development files
 Modern Intel SoCs automatically record hardware state during fatal crashes,
 such as machine check exceptions, triple faults or unexpected resets, into
 on-die memory.
 .
 This package provides the C and C++ headers, the pkg-config file and the
 symbolic link needed to build applications against the Intel Crash Log
 library.

Package: intel-crashlog-efi
Architecture: amd64
Build-Profiles: <pkg.intel-crashlog.efi>
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Static-Built-Using: ${Static-Built-Using}
Description: Extract Intel Crash Log records from the UEFI shell
 Modern Intel SoCs automatically record hardware state during fatal crashes,
 such as machine check exceptions, triple faults or unexpected resets, into
 on-die memory.
 .
 This package provides iclg.efi, a UEFI application that extracts those records
 from the ACPI Boot Error Record Table before an operating system is started,
 and either saves them on an EFI system partition or displays them on the UEFI
 console. The application is not run on the installed system: copy it to a
 FAT32 partition and start it from the UEFI shell.
